{"id": "De3zfY-xTiZ", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Sita dropped her jewels from the sky. Guess WHO found them? 💛 Ravana Takes Sita | Ramayan Part 7 of 12\n\n🚪 Sita welcomed a holy man as her guest. Then he showed his true face: Ravana. \"Be my queen!\" he said. Sita answered: \"A jackal wants a lioness?\" (Aranya Kanda 46–47)\n🫏 He grabbed her, and his golden chariot rose into the sky, pulled by… donkeys! Sita cried to the trees, the river, the deer: \"Tell Ram!\" (Aranya 49)\n🦅 Old Jatayu, the eagle king, fought for her, until Ravana cut his wings. (Aranya 50–51)\n💛 Over a hill, Sita saw five monkeys. She tied her jewels in her scarf, and dropped them. (Aranya 54)\n😢 Ram came home to an empty hut. He searched everywhere, calling her name. He found Jatayu dying. With his last breath: \"Ravana took her.\" Ram cremated him like his own father. (Aranya 60–68)\n🐒 And those five monkeys on the hill? One of them was HANUMAN. (Kishkindha 6)\n\n➡️ Part 8: Ram meets Hanuman, and the arrow from behind a tree. Follow @therishikatha so you don't miss it!\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. Insta Family Sale on Books 1–3, till 25 Oct → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 Comment JAI SHRI RAM if you're watching the whole series 🙏\n🔖 Save this, and share it with a Hanuman bhakt\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #sitaharan #jatayu #hanuman #ravana #valmikiramayana #jaishriram #sanatandharma #hindumythology #indianmythology #ramayanseries #kidsbooks #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792834065, "like_count": 1289, "comment_count": 20, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-859921783849920a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 51.665, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f